    }
  ],
  "content": [
    {
      "id": "introduction",
      "title": "Introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">A technique for looking at a&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">chunk of an array</strong><span style=\"letter-spacing: -0.003em;\">&nbsp;at a time and sliding that chunk from left to right instead of recomputing from scratch every step.</span>",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "1-the-idea",
      "title": "1. The Idea",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Imagine a frame sliding across the array. At every position, the frame shows you a portion of the data that's your window.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250835721-786172273.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250835721-786172273.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250835721-786172273.png",
          "alt": "Sliding window starting position over an array"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "window starts here",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785250837437-208278575.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": [],
          "content": null
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "slides one step →<strong>4 leaves, 1 enters</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "<img src=\"/engineering/dsa-media/1785250838995-570162347.png\" alt=\"image.png\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; margin: 16px 0px; border-radius: 4px;\">",
          "items": [],
          "content": null
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "slides again →<strong>2 leaves, 5 enters</strong>",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "text": "<strong>Key insight:&nbsp;</strong>only one element changes on each side per step so you update your answer in O(1) instead of recomputing the whole window every time.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "divider",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2-two-types",
      "title": "2. Two Types",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "1. Fixed Size Window",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The window size&nbsp;<strong>k is given</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Both pointers move forward together while keeping the window size constant.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use this when the problem asks for a&nbsp;<strong>subarray or substring of size k</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "heading2",
          "text": "2. Variable Size Window",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The window size&nbsp;<strong>can grow or shrink</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The right pointer expands the window, and the left pointer moves only when the condition breaks.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Use this for problems like&nbsp;<strong>longest or shortest valid subarray/substring</strong>.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "items": [],
          "url": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250840429-328514688.png",
          "caption": "",
          "content": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250840429-328514688.png",
          "text": "/engineering/dsa-media/1785250840429-328514688.png",
          "alt": "Fixed size window versus variable size window"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We cover both in full detail in the next two sections.",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "",
          "items": []
